      "key": {
        "uuid": "b4c619d3_85081773",
        "filename": "include/core/SkRecorder.h",
        "patchSetId": 26
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-24T13:19:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Mostly bringing this up for discussion and less about things that need to happen in this CL.\n\nDo we think we\u0027ll have public APIs in Skia that will pass in a backend specific Recorder (i.e. a skgpu::Recorder or SkRasterRecorder)? I know were trying to merge as much as we can but maybe there are still something that should be very specific to a backend. If that is the case do we want this base class to also have virtuals for things like asGraphiteRecorder() and asRasterRecorder()?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "827704676338938881bfe2646de1452e936b32fe",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3b6e4db0_4d1b0581",
        "filename": "include/core/SkRecorder.h",
        "patchSetId": 26
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-25T21:10:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t know if we want those to be public. In my opinion, the client should be holding on to the recorder of the sub type, so they shouldn\u0027t need to call those virtuals. We can add them if we find a usecase.",
      "parentUuid": "b4c619d3_85081773",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "827704676338938881bfe2646de1452e936b32fe",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a61a5464_4382dd3b",
